  <h1>Seat Sherpa vs FlixBus and Greyhound</h1>
  <div class="meta">Updated September 2026 · Prices are typical ranges; live seat prices are on each route page</div>

  <p class="lede"><strong>Short answer:</strong> the prices are close. A bus ticket from San Francisco to Los Angeles is roughly $25 to $70 depending on how early you book; a Seat Sherpa carpool seat is capped at $55 plus a 5% fee. The differences are time and logistics: the carpool is door to door and typically 1 to 3 hours faster, while the bus runs on a fixed timetable whether or not anyone has posted your route.</p>

  <h2>Side by side</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Seat Sherpa</th><th>FlixBus / Greyhound</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>SF to LA fare</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">$30 to $55 + 5% fee</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">$25 to $70</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LA to Las Vegas fare</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">$25 to $55 + 5% fee</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">$25 to $60</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LA to San Diego fare</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">$15 to $30 + 5% fee</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">$15 to $35</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SF to LA door to door</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa">6 to 7.5 h</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">8 to 10 h with transfers to and from stations</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pickup</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa">A spot you agree in chat: a BART or Metro station, a campus, a parking lot</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">Fixed terminal or curbside stop</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Departure</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">The driver’s time; drivers post the week of the trip, often several per day on busy corridors</td><td class="win" data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">Timetabled, many departures a day</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Luggage</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">By arrangement; look for the large-trunk or ski-rack badge on the ride</td><td class="win" data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">One checked bag plus a carry-on included</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Who you travel with</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">One verified driver and up to a few passengers, with reviews</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">A full coach</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cancellation</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">24h+ full seat refund, 2 to 24h 50%, driver cancels 100%</td><td data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">Varies by fare type; cheapest fares are often non-refundable</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Overnight</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa">Rare</td><td class="win" data-l="FlixBus / Greyhound">Overnight coaches exist on SF to LA</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>How to decide</h2>
  <p>Check the route page first. If a driver has posted a time that works, the carpool is faster and starts closer to your door. If nothing is posted yet, either set a route alert so you are emailed the moment a ride appears, post a request on the <a href="/requests">ride request board</a> (drivers read it before deciding what to post), or take the bus. On holiday weekends the bus sells out and prices climb, while carpool seats stay capped.</p>

  <div class="callout" style="text-align:center">
    <h3>See live seat prices on your route</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom:6px">Drivers post trips they are already taking. Book in the browser or the app; no account needed to look.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/rides?c=compare">Browse rides →</a>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:#8a8a92;margin-top:10px">Driving somewhere yourself? <a href="/post">Post the ride</a> and split the cost.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is carpooling cheaper than FlixBus?</h3><p>About the same on most California routes. FlixBus is cheapest booked weeks ahead; a Seat Sherpa seat is capped at $55 regardless of when you book, so it tends to win on short notice and on holiday weekends when bus fares rise.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is a Seat Sherpa ride faster than Greyhound?</h3><p>Usually by 1 to 3 hours on San Francisco to Los Angeles, because there are no station transfers and no intermediate stops beyond the ones the driver has listed. Both depend on I-5 traffic.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Does the bus go from Los Angeles to Las Vegas?</h3><p>Yes, FlixBus and Greyhound both run it, typically 5.5 to 7 hours for $25 to $60. A carpool seat on Seat Sherpa is typically $25 to $55 plus a 5% fee and 4.5 to 5.5 hours.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>How much does a Seat Sherpa seat cost?</h3><p>It depends on the route and the driver, but every seat has a hard cap: the IRS standard mileage rate (about $0.76 per mile in 2026) multiplied by the drivable miles, divided across the seats, and never more than $55 a seat. Riders pay the seat price plus a 5% service fee, shown before you pay. Live prices for each corridor are on the route pages and in the ride browser.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is Seat Sherpa safe?</h3><p>Every driver verifies a phone number by SMS, uploads a driver’s license that is checked for expiry, registers the vehicle, and connects a Stripe account that verifies identity and bank details. Riders see the driver’s photo, trip count and reviews before booking, can filter for women drivers, and can block anyone. A 4-digit pickup code confirms the rider got in the car and is what releases payment.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>What is the cancellation policy?</h3><p>One standard policy on every ride: cancel 24 or more hours before departure for a full seat refund, 2 to 24 hours before for 50%, and inside 2 hours there is no refund. The 5% service fee is non-refundable when the rider cancels. If the driver cancels, the rider gets 100% back including the fee.</p></div>

